the-firm-as-one-program-56 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-56 = unlines (cons "- **Q3** The quant's job is the reduction of uncertainty about unobserved (often future) events." (cons "  Predicting the vehicle count in a retail parking lot on a given day and predicting a market price are instances of the same inference problem; framing quantitative research around price series alone misstates the problem." (cons "  - **Q3.1** The problem: given environmental data, forecast subsequent environment states. The environment is the earth, the physical universe, with myriad inseparable activity within it." (cons "  - **Q3.2** Every equity, commodity and future corresponds to physical events in the real world." (cons "  - **Q3.3** Pricing is a byproduct, an observation, of complete world state. [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)]" nil)))))
